  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nWarmer and drier conditions will generally dominate the forecast\nperiod beginning today. Saturday will be the exception, with a\ncold front bringing temperatures down into the 60s to low 70sF \ninstead of 70s to 80sF today and Sunday into next week. Winds will\nincrease with the front out of the north-northwest, with gusts in\nthe teens and 20s mph. Other than far southeast Montana, breezy\nwinds will diminish into the afternoon.\n\nThe chance for precipitation today through the weekend is very\nlow, with sprinkles to a weak shower or two possible early\nSaturday morning with the frontal passage.\n\nUpper ridging will take hold over the Northern Rockies next week,\nkeeping the aforementioned warm and dry conditions through at\nleast the first week of October. Monday looks to be the warmest\nday of the week with highs in the 80sF. Due to this period of\nabove normal temperatures and dry conditions, fire weather\nconcerns may begin to increase. This is especially true for\nlocations that did not receive as much precipitation with the\nwidespread rain event in mid-September. Additionally, periodic\ncold fronts may bring increased winds which could exacerbate\nalready dry conditions.\n\nMatos",
